WEBVTT

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.305
President Clinton,
if you're here: thank you.

00:09:02.329 --> 00:09:04.035
(Laughter)

00:09:04.059 --> 00:09:05.210
So the question is:

00:09:05.234 --> 00:09:09.429
Why are so many people so wrong
about something so important?

00:09:09.453 --> 00:09:11.279
I think there are a number of reasons.

00:09:11.303 --> 00:09:13.216
One of them is we have better reporting.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.930
The Associated Press
is a better chronicler of wars

00:09:16.954 --> 00:09:18.395
over the surface of the earth

00:09:18.419 --> 00:09:20.327
than 16th-century monks were.

00:09:20.351 --> 00:09:21.387
(Laughter)

00:09:21.411 --> 00:09:22.819
There's a cognitive illusion.

00:09:22.843 --> 00:09:24.921
We cognitive psychologists know

00:09:24.945 --> 00:09:30.249
that the easier it is to recall
specific instances of something,